      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{7x+11} & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no root.",
