      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{17-2x} & =-3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[5]{17-2x})^{5} & =(-3)^{5} \\\\ 17-2x & =-243 \\\\ -2x & =-260 \\\\ x & =130\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=130.$",
