      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x}+2.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x}+2=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x}+2 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{-8-3x} & =-2 \\\\ (\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x})^{9} & =(-2)^{9} \\\\ -8-3x & =-512 \\\\ -3x & =-504 \\\\ x & =168\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=168.$",
